#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:217
msgid "Key Rotation Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:219
msgid "**Before rotation**: Data is encrypted and decrypted with ``key``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:220
msgid ""
"**Start rotation**: Move current ``key`` value to ``previousKeys`` array,"
" set new value for ``key``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:221
msgid ""
"**During rotation**: New data encrypted with new ``key``, old data still "
"decryptable via ``previousKeys``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:222
msgid ""
"**Re-encrypt data** (optional): Decrypt and re-encrypt existing data with"
" the new key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:223
msgid ""
"**Complete rotation**: Once all data is re-encrypted, remove old keys "
"from ``previousKeys``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:225
msgid ""
"The ``previousKeys`` feature is for **decryption fallback only**. All new"
" encryption operations always use the current ``key``. If you pass an "
"explicit key via the ``$params`` argument to ``encrypt()`` or "
"``decrypt()``, the previousKeys fallback will not be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:230
msgid "Padding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:232
msgid ""
"Sometimes, the length of a message may provide a lot of information about"
" its nature. If a message is one of \"yes\", \"no\" and \"maybe\", "
"encrypting the message doesn't help: knowing the length is enough to know"
" what the message is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:236
msgid ""
"Padding is a technique to mitigate this, by making the length a multiple "
"of a given block size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:238
msgid ""
"Padding is implemented in ``SodiumHandler`` using libsodium's native "
"``sodium_pad`` and ``sodium_unpad`` functions. This requires the use of a"
" padding length (in bytes) that is added to the plaintext message prior "
"to encryption, and removed after decryption. Padding is configurable via "
"the ``$blockSize`` property of ``Config\\Encryption``. This value should "
"be greater than zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/encryption.rst:243
msgid ""
"You are advised not to devise your own padding implementation. You must "
"always use the more secure implementation of a library. Also, passwords "
"should not be padded. Usage of padding in order to hide the length of a "
"password is not recommended. A client willing to send a password to a "
"server should hash it instead (even with a single iteration of the hash "
"function). This ensures that the length of the transmitted data is "
"constant, and that the server doesn't effortlessly get a copy of the "
"password."
msgstr ""

